 INPUT CARD>! equation (the hydrate has one more O and two more H than the bare             
 INPUT CARD>! aldehyde). A single water molecule embedded in a PCM continuum is a           
 INPUT CARD>! standard, if approximate, way to estimate water's chemical potential --       
 INPUT CARD>! it does not fully capture bulk liquid water's extensive hydrogen-bonded       
 INPUT CARD>! structure, but is a reasonable and widely-used approximation, and will be     
 INPUT CARD>! applied consistently across both the acetaldehyde calibration and the         
 INPUT CARD>! chloroacetaldehyde case.                                                      
